{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F3yuEoDbsWZ2QdcLno8xmG","type":"tool_result","content":"=== E10.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E10.1\",\n  \"check\": \"The gateway, tool services, and delegated workers each write audit records with all six identity fields and the shared trace context.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find audit writers in the gateway, tool services, and delegated workers. 2) Check each writes all six identity fields and the shared trace context. 3) Answer no if any component writes records without them or starts a new trace. Answer unknown if a component's code is outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== E10.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"E10.2\",\n  \"check\": \"The agent's credentials have no permission to delete, update, or overwrite audit records (for example an append-only or WORM store with IAM denies).\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the agent's IAM role or database grants and the audit store config. 2) Check the agent has no delete, update, or overwrite rights (`DeleteObject`, overwriting `PutObject`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`) and the store is append-only or WORM (Object Lock). 3) Answer no if the agent's credentials can delete or rewrite records, or grant `*`. Answer unknown if these are set outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== E10.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"E10.3\",\n  \"check\": \"No tool or peer the agent can call is able to delete or rewrite audit records on its behalf, or such requests are held for approval under B05.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) List the tools and peers the agent can call. 2) For each, check whether it can delete or rewrite audit records (database admin, log management, storage tools). 3) Answer no if any can and such requests are not held for approval under B05.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== E10.4\n{\n  \"id\": \"E10.4\",\n  \"check\": \"Calls into vendor services are mapped from the gateway's verified identity and correlation ID to the vendor's job or receipt ID.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find calls into vendor services. 2) Check the gateway stores its verified identity and correlation ID together with the vendor's job or receipt ID. 3) Answer no if the vendor ID is not stored, or stored without the link to identity and correlation ID.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== E11.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E11.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Audit retention is set in config to cover the investigation window and the legal minimum (for example at least six months for EU AI Act high-risk systems).\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find retention settings for audit storage: bucket lifecycle rules, log retention days, TTLs. 2) Check the value covers the investigation window and the legal minimum (for example six months for EU AI Act high-risk systems). 3) Answer no if retention is shorter or unset. Answer unknown if audit storage is configured outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== E11.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"E11.2\",\n  \"check\": \"Access to audit records is limited by role, and redaction rules apply to sensitive fields.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find IAM policies or ACLs on audit storage. 2) Check reads are limited by role. 3) Check redaction rules apply to sensitive fields. 4) Answer no if read access is broad (`*`, all engineers) or no redaction exists.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== E11.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"E11.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Integrity protection (hash chain, signatures, or WORM) plus sequence numbers or delivery receipts let missing records be detected, with an alert on gaps or pipeline failure.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit writer and store config. 2) Check for integrity protection (hash chain, signatures, or WORM) plus sequence numbers or delivery receipts. 3) Check an alert fires on gaps or pipeline failure. 4) Answer no if any piece is missing, or a hash is computed but never verified.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== E11.4\n{\n  \"id\": \"E11.4\",\n  \"check\": \"High-impact actions are blocked when required audit capture is down.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find high-impact action paths. 2) Check they confirm audit capture is working before the action runs. 3) Answer no if audit write errors are caught and the action proceeds, or the audit record is written only after success.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n     1\t\"\"\"Runtime settings, read once from the environment at process start.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport os\n     5\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n     6\tfrom functools import lru_cache\n     7\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     8\t\n     9\timport yaml\n    10\t\n    11\t\n    12\tdef _env(name: str, default: str | None = None) -> str:\n    13\t    value = os.environ.get(name, default)\n    14\t    if value is None:\n    15\t        raise RuntimeError(f\"missing required setting {name}\")\n    16\t    return value\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    20\tclass Settings:\n    21\t    database_url: str\n    22\t    erp_mcp_url: str\n    23\t    payments_api_url: str\n    24\t    slack_api_url: str\n    25\t    sts_url: str\n    26\t    oidc_issuer: str\n    27\t    oidc_audience: str\n    28\t    oidc_jwks_url: str\n    29\t    workload_token_path: str\n    30\t    slack_signing_secret_path: str\n    31\t    mail_gateway_hmac_path: str\n    32\t    model_id: str\n    33\t    extractor_model_id: str\n    34\t    manifest_path: Path\n    35\t    prompt_dir: Path\n    36\t    policy_path: Path\n    37\t    tools_path: Path\n    38\t    operational_owner: str\n    39\t    image_digest: str\n    40\t\n    41\t    @property\n    42\t    def policy(self) -> dict:\n    43\t        return _load_yaml(self.policy_path)\n    44\t\n    45\t    @property\n    46\t    def manifest(self) -> dict:\n    47\t        return _load_yaml(self.manifest_path)\n    48\t\n    49\t    @property\n    50\t    def budgets(self) -> dict:\n    51\t        return self.policy[\"budgets\"]\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef _load_yaml(path: Path) -> dict:\n    55\t    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n    56\t        return yaml.safe_load(fh)\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n    60\tdef get_settings() -> Settings:\n    61\t    root = Path(_env(\"APP_ROOT\", \"/app\"))\n    62\t    return Settings(\n    63\t        database_url=_env(\"DATABASE_URL\"),\n    64\t        erp_mcp_url=_env(\"ERP_MCP_URL\"),\n    65\t        payments_api_url=_env(\"PAYMENTS_API_URL\"),\n    66\t        slack_api_url=_env(\"SLACK_API_URL\", \"https://slack.com/api\"),\n    67\t        sts_url=_env(\"STS_URL\"),\n    68\t        oidc_issuer=_env(\"OIDC_ISSUER\"),\n    69\t        oidc_audience=_env(\"OIDC_AUDIENCE\", \"procurement-agent\"),\n    70\t        oidc_jwks_url=_env(\"OIDC_JWKS_URL\"),\n    71\t        workload_token_path=_env(\n    72\t            \"WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/tokens/procurement-agent\"\n    73\t        ),\n    74\t        slack_signing_secret_path=_env(\n    75\t            \"SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/slack/signing-secret\"\n    76\t        ),\n    77\t        mail_gateway_hmac_path=_env(\n    78\t            \"MAIL_GATEWAY_HMAC_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/mail/hmac-key\"\n    79\t        ),\n    80\t        model_id=_env(\"MODEL_ID\"),\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\tdef clean_outbound(text: str) -> str:\n    17\t    return strip_unapproved_links(redact_text(text))[:MAX_TEXT]\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\tclass SlackClient:\n    21\t    def __init__(self, api_url: str, bot_token_provider):\n    22\t        self.api_url = api_url\n    23\t        self._token = bot_token_provider\n    24\t\n    25\t    async def post(self, channel: str, text: str, blocks: list | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    26\t        payload: dict[str, Any] = {\n    27\t            \"channel\": channel,\n    28\t            \"text\": clean_outbound(text),\n    29\t            \"unfurl_links\": False,\n    30\t            \"unfurl_media\": False,\n    31\t            \"mrkdwn\": True,\n    32\t        }\n    33\t        if blocks:\n    34\t            payload[\"blocks\"] = blocks\n    35\t        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=10.0, follow_redirects=False) as client:\n    36\t            resp = await client.post(\n    37\t                f\"{self.api_url}/chat.postMessage\",\n    38\t                headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {await self._token()}\"},\n    39\t                json=payload,\n    40\t            )\n    41\t        resp.raise_for_status()\n    42\t        body = resp.json()\n    43\t        if not body.get(\"ok\"):\n    44\t            raise RuntimeError(f\"slack error: {body.get('error')}\")\n    45\t        return {\"channel\": body[\"channel\"], \"ts\": body[\"ts\"]}\n    46\t\n    47\t    async def post_approval_request(\n    48\t        self, *, tenant: str, approval_id: str, tool: str, target: str, summary: dict, expires_at: datetime\n    49\t    ) -> None:\n    50\t        lines = \"\\n\".join(f\"• *{k}*: `{v}`\" for k, v in summary.items())\n    51\t        text = f\"Approval needed for `{tool}` on `{target}` (expires {expires_at:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M} UTC)\\n{lines}\"\n    52\t        await self.post(\n    53\t            channel=f\"#approvals-{tenant}\",\n    54\t            text=text,\n    55\t            blocks=[\n    56\t                {\"type\": \"section\", \"text\": {\"type\": \"mrkdwn\", \"text\": clean_outbound(text)}},\n    57\t                {\n    58\t                    \"type\": \"actions\",\n    59\t                    \"elements\": [\n    60\t                        {\"type\": \"button\", \"action_id\": \"approve\", \"value\": approval_id, \"text\": {\"type\": \"plain_text\", \"text\": \"Approve\"}, \"style\": \"primary\"},\n    61\t                        {\"type\": \"button\", \"action_id\": \"reject\", \"value\": approval_id, \"text\": {\"type\": \"plain_text\", \"text\": \"Reject\"}, \"style\": \"danger\"},\n    62\t                    ],\n    63\t                },\n    64\t            ],\n    65\t        )\n    66\t\napp/ingest.py:80:def scan_for_injection(text: str) -> list[str]:\napp/ingest.py:98:        findings = scan_for_injection(text)\napp/ingest.py:100:            raise Rejected(\"possible prompt injection: \" + \"; \".join(findings))\n# Release manifest for the procurement agent. Regenerated by CI on every\n# release build (see .github/workflows/ci.yaml, job \"release\").\nrelease: \"procurement-agent 2026.09.4\"\nowner: team-procurement-platform\n\nimage:\n  repository: registry.example-corp.test/procurement/agent\n  digest: \"sha256:7c1e4a0f9b3d2e85a6c4f1b0d9e8a7c6b5d4e3f2a1b0c9d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0\"\n  sbom: \"registry.example-corp.test/procurement/agent:sha256-7c1e4a0f9b3d2e85a6c4f1b0d9e8a7c6b5d4e3f2a1b0c9d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0.sbom\"\n  signer:\n    issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    subject: \"https://github.com/example-corp/procurement-agent/.github/workflows/ci.yaml@refs/heads/main\"\n\nharness:\n  source_commit: \"3f9a1c7e2b8d4f6a0c5e9b1d7f3a8c2e6b4d0f91\"\n  digest: \"sha256:5b2d8f1a9c3e7b0d4f6a2c8e1b5d9f3a7c0e4b8d2f6a1c5e9b3d7f0a4c8e2b6d\"\n\nprompts:\n  system:\n    path: prompts/system.md\n    sha256: \"sha256:dcf69216667e65a0be3711d99aac81b707ba843296e7ce26d6fcbdb50c5bcc50\"\n  extractor:\n    path: prompts/extractor.md\n    sha256: \"sha256:6ef6527b77ffcca8851e7a8760e6373f3daede15d5b343b878737f0deec28de3\"\n\nconfig:\n  policy:\n    path: config/policy.yaml\n    version: \"proc-policy-2026.09.3\"\n    sha256: \"sha256:d6a55f1e170bdd457958243ddd9aa938f4ca707a3e1e9d1e7bca2a54df33ad32\"\n  tools:\n    path: config/tools.yaml\n    sha256: \"sha256:86dccc3d7d166bf8e131c3b2afbe5f2b846a57eaaf087b55f9e308844eda9400\"\n  network_policy: deploy/k8s/networkpol