{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDUGzTVLS8gpAErczJEW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E10, E11 and E12 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator printed \"Valid\" (`--batch E10,E11,E12 --before-challenges`, with `--fix`, which changed nothing). I did not run challenges, and I added no other items. I found no injection attempts.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| E10 (G1) | gap | E10.1, E10.2 and E10.4 are `no`. E10.3 is `yes`. |\n| E11 (G2) | gap | E11.3 is `no`. E11.4 is `yes`. E11.1 and E11.2 are `unknown`. |\n| E12 (G3) | needs_evidence | The item has no checks, because code can't show a fleet incident drill. |\n\n**E10**\n- **E10.1:** The agent loop and the extractor sub-agent write all six identity fields, and the sub-agent keeps `trace_id`. But the ERP gateway call carries only `business_unit` and `run_id` (`app/mcp_client.py:125`). The payments and Slack calls carry no trace header either.\n- **E10.2:** `audit_events` is `SELECT, INSERT` only for the agent role. But the agent role can `UPDATE` the `approvals` table (`migrations/001_init.sql:122`). Approval decisions are never written to `audit_events`, so that table is their only record.\n- **E10.3:** Only `app/audit.py` touches `audit_events`. None of the nine tools or the extractor can delete or rewrite audit rows.\n- **E10.4:** The vendor receipt is stored on success. If a payment errors after the vendor accepted it, the error row has no vendor id (`app/loop.py:91`). The idempotency key isn't stored, and the model provider's response id isn't recorded.\n\n**E11**\n- **E11.1 and E11.2:** Retention and who can read the audit store are set outside this repo. Redaction is applied to audit payloads, but it only matches patterns inside string values, not sensitive key names.\n- **E11.3:** There is no hash chain, signature, sequence number or gap alert. The only alert is the budget-exceeded Slack post.\n- **E11.4:** Every tool call awaits the `tool_proposed` and `authz_decision` audit writes before the tool runs, and nothing catches a failed write.\n\nThe 7 prescan hits all belong to other items (B07, B08, B09, B11, R05), so I left them for those batches. The scope field says what I couldn't see: ERP gateway and payments service code, audit store retention and reader permissions, alerting rules and incident runbooks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1431,"cache_read_input_tokens":91044,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1431},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4d2f1d4-6d27-449e-9a69-d554d089643e","uuid":"543d3f95-fddf-481d-af3a-100243904bb2","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:14:48.773Z","request_id":"req_011CgDUGz8PjqhLK5DCtZAh8"}
